  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## AI Security Tool Design  \r\n\r\nThis chatbot is an AI systems design assistant trained to help you create and refine ideas for AI-powered cybersecurity tools that address real network vulnerabilities.  \r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Think about the vulnerabilities you identified on Day 1.  \r\n2. Ask the chatbot:  \r\n   - What problem should this AI tool solve in my network?  \r\n   - Who will use or be affected by this tool?  \r\n   - What data or systems does it rely on?  \r\n   - What are its strengths and limitations?  \r\n   - How might this tool create new risks or ethical concerns?  \r\n3. Record the AI’s ideas and your **revisions or critiques** in your **AI Security Tool Design Organizer.**\r\n\r\n::: details [**Need help refining your questions?**]\r\nUse these prompts to get more specific or useful responses from the AI:\r\n- Can you give an example of how this AI would detect or prevent a threat?\r\n- What kind of data would this AI need access to?\r\n- How could human oversight make this system safer or more reliable?\r\n- What unintended consequences might this design have?\r\n- How can this AI tool be transparent and ethical?\r\n:::\r\n",
    "aichat_settings": {
      "initialCustomizations": {
        "selectedModelId": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "temperature": 0.3,
        "systemPrompt": "",
        "retrievalContexts": [

        ],
        "modelCardInfo": {
          "botName": "AI Security Tool Design Assistant",
          "description": "The AI Security Tool Design Assistant is a specialized chatbot that helps students design, evaluate, and refine AI-powered cybersecurity tools. It guides users through creating feasible, ethical, and clearly defined AI systems that address real network vulnerabilities. The chatbot supports structured, three-part responses that include:\n\nAn AI Tool Concept describing how the tool functions and who uses it.\n\nA Risks & Limitations section identifying challenges such as bias, privacy, or overreliance on automation.\n\nRefinement Recommendations suggesting how to improve the design for fairness, transparency, and human oversight.\n\nThis chatbot promotes creativity, critical thinking, and ethical awareness while helping students connect AI design decisions to real-world cybersecurity challenges.",
          "intendedUse": "- Educational design assistant for students developing AI-based cybersecurity tools\n- Support for project-based learning on AI design, ethics, and risk assessment\n- Classroom tool for guided inquiry into how AI mitigates network vulnerabilities\n- Discussion aid for evaluating AI system feasibility, risks, and limitations\n- Resource for teaching Designing AI and Managing AI competencies ",
          "limitationsAndWarnings": "- Not a real design engine – The AI does not build or code functional systems; it generates conceptual designs only.\n- Not real-time cybersecurity software – It does not monitor, analyze, or detect actual network activity.\n- No hacking or security circumvention – The chatbot must reject any request related to unauthorized access, exploitation, or hacking.\n- Educational scope only – Responses must remain within the context of classroom learning and ethical AI development.\n- Human judgment required – Students are encouraged to critique and refine AI-generated ideas rather than accept them uncritically.",
          "testingAndEvaluation": "- Accuracy Testing: Confirm that AI responses clearly describe feasible AI system designs, not speculative or fictional technologies.\n- Bias Testing: Ensure the AI discusses ethical and fairness implications, acknowledging bias and human oversight needs.\n- Feasibility Testing: Validate that suggestions are realistic for educational contexts and not technically impossible or unsafe.\n- Clarity Testing: Check that language is student-friendly and free of unnecessary jargon.\n- Educational Effectiveness: Collect classroom feedback to improve question framing, scaffold design thinking, and ensure alignment with project outcomes.",
          "exampleTopics": [
            "Design an AI tool that helps detect insider threats in a hospital network.",
            "What data would an AI need to identify phishing emails before users open them?",
            "How can human oversight improve an AI system that detects malware?",
            "What are the ethical risks of an AI that monitors employee activity?",
            "Suggest improvements to my AI tool that protects customer data during online transactions."
          ],
          "isPublished": false
        }
      },
      "visibilities": {
        "selectedModelId": "hidden",
